<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Friday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*  *G*   *H*</p>
<p>Jun 04  21,454 5,911 27,365 13,870 13,890 6,132  0  20,022</p>
<p>Jun 05  21,536 5,709 27,245 14,085 14,103 6,099  0  20,202</p>
<p>Jun 06  21,488 5,782 27,270 14,247 14,264 5,888  0  20,152</p>
<p>Jun 10  21,709 5,588 27,297 14,233 14,267 6,081  0  20,348</p>
<p>Jun 11  21,911 5,555 27,466 14,100 14,130 6,406  0  20,536</p>
<p>Jun 12  21,886 5,529 27,415 13,998 14,030 6,461  0  20,491</p>
<p>Jun 13  21,836 5,533 27,369 13,876 13,907 6,511  0  20,418</p>
<p>Jun 17  21,811 5,319 27,130 13,808 13,841 6,388  0  20,229</p>
<p>Jun 18  21.576 5,435 27,011 13,659 13,689 6,376  0  20.065</p>
<p>*A  Of the $21.58 billion in international reserves, $1.84 billion (8.53 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0651))</p>
</text>
